---
import BaseLayout from "astro-blog-theme/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How erik-skopp.de handles personal data."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Erik Skopp (private, non-commercial blog). Further details in the
      <a href="/impressum/">legal notice</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This website is a static site. It sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, loads
      <strong>no external fonts, scripts or CDNs</strong> at runtime and uses
      <strong>no analytics or tracking services</strong>. Personal data is
      essentially only processed in the server log files.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server log files</h2>
    <p>
      The website runs on a server operated by netcup GmbH (location: Nuremberg,
      Germany). When the pages are accessed, the web server automatically
      collects data transmitted by your browser and stores it in log files:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>abbreviated or full IP address</li>
      <li>date and time of access</li>
      <li>requested address (URL) and HTTP status code</li>
      <li>amount of data transferred</li>
      <li>referrer URL (the previously visited page)</li>
      <li>browser type and operating system (user agent)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in
      providing the website reliably and securely (including detecting and
      fending off attack attempts). Log data is deleted after 14 days at the
      latest, unless it is needed longer to investigate a specific
      security-relevant incident. Fail2ban is used to ward off automated attacks
      and temporarily blocks suspicious IP addresses.
    </p>

    <h2>Encryption</h2>
    <p>
      The connection to the website is encrypted with TLS (HTTPS). The
      certificate is issued by Let’s Encrypt.
    </p>

    <h2>Local storage in your browser (localStorage)</h2>
    <p>
      The website remembers your preference for the light or dark appearance in
      your browser’s <code>localStorage</code>. This value stays exclusively on
      your device, is not transmitted to the server and can be deleted by you at
      any time via your browser settings. It is not a cookie and not tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>
      The search runs entirely in your browser. It loads an index file
      (<code>/search.json</code>) from this server once; the search terms are
      neither transmitted nor stored.
    </p>

    <h2>RSS feed</h2>
    <p>
      The RSS feed (<a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a>) is served as a static file
      from this server. The same information applies as under “server log
      files”.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      This blog does not offer a contact form. If you send me a message by some
      other means, I process your details solely to handle the enquiry
      (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) and delete them once the enquiry has been dealt with.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Posts may contain links to external websites. When you click them you are
      taken to third-party servers whose data processing is the responsibility
      of the respective provider. External links open in a new browser tab.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the following rights towards the controller:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access to the data stored about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>objection to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
      supervisory authority about the processing of your personal data (Art. 77
      GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>This privacy policy is dated August 2026.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
